  "body": "## What changed\n\n`detect_pockets` returned no feature for the reported slot (p01-flange). This PR finds two causes and fixes both, in `crates/app/src/recognize`:\n\n1. **A hole tangent to the slot wall.** The through holes at x 39..45 touch the slot wall at x 45. So the hole ring and the outer ring of the floor share one vertex. The feature walk (`geometry::feature::build_loops`) reports each ring through such a vertex as `Open`, so the floor had no outer ring and the reader skipped it. The new `recognize::pinch` takes the walk's split rings as the outer ring and its holes, but only when it can prove them:\n   - each ring is simple, and each span of each ring is a boundary edge of the face;\n   - each hole has a vertex off the outer ring, and those vertices are inside the largest ring;\n   - the largest ring's area less the hole areas is the face's facet area (relative slack 1e-3).\n\n   Any other knotted face stays refused, as before. The geometry walk does not change, so no `FaceId` moves.\n2. **A hole through the slot floor.** `slot_of` refused each floor with an inner ring. Now it refuses a floor with a boss only: an inner ring with a facet above the floor on one of its edges (`walls::Mesh::rises_from`). A hole has its wall below the floor, so the floor still reads as a slot. `islands` still counts every inner ring.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/2440-slot-floor-holes.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe issue's part was rebuilt in SolidCraft (plate 100 x 60 x 10, slot x 35..45 with its floor at z 7, four 6 mm through holes at (±42, ±22)) and exported as STL. It was then read through `camcraft-cli mcp`.\n\n- Before: `{\"count\": 0, \"features\": []}`.\n- After: one `slot`, floor z 7, top z 10, `islands` 2, width 10, length 60, ends `[\"open\", \"open\"]`, centreline x 40 from y 30 to y −30.\n- `detect_pockets {create: 0}` makes `Slot1`. With the stock fitted to the part, `generate` is ok, `verify` has no finding, and `post` writes 34 lines.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/mcp_pockets.rs`)\n\n- `a_slot_with_a_hole_tangent_to_its_wall_is_still_a_slot`: a hand-built, watertight block whose diamond hole touches the slot wall at one vertex. The test checks the slot, its ends, its width, its length and its floor area (400 − 18). It also checks that `create` makes a Slot that generates.\n- `a_slot_with_holes_through_its_floor_is_still_a_slot`: a height field with two holes in the floor (no tangency).\n- `a_boss_standing_in_the_channel_is_not_a_slot`: the same field with bosses. It is still an open pocket, as before.\n\nThe first two fail on `upstream/main` and pass with this change. The boss test passes on both, so it guards against a fix that counts every inner ring as a hole.\n\n## Gates\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 5 steps, 0 failed (`app suites: mcp_pockets`, `app suites: pocket_recognition` and the build steps).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-app -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches 74 app heavy steps. They are not run yet. I will add the result in a comment before the PR is flagged ready.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A knotted face whose split fails the proof. It stays refused by code reading only; no test builds such a face.\n- The UI Pockets page. It reads the same `recognize::pockets_of`, so it lists the same slots.\n\nChangelog: `detect_pockets` now lists a slot whose floor has holes through it, also when a hole is tangent to the slot wall (#2440).\n\nFixes #2440\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
